  "published": "2026-09-09T19:41:05.313Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.9.10 — Expose the H264Nal Annex-B helper (public) with an allocation-free IsKeyframe, so an integrator forwarding raw H.264 to a browser (WebCodecs) can label keyframes without re-implementing NAL scanning. Additive, no API breaks.\n\n0.9.9 — Since 0.9.0, all verified on real Windows/Linux/macOS hardware: 3-OS audio plus two-way audio (operator mic → host), an audio jitter buffer, cursor overlay (incl. macOS NSCursor), adaptive quality with dynamic H.264 bitrate, sequence-numbered loss recovery, auto-reconnect, multi-monitor (enumerate + switch), macOS clipboard, viewer→host file upload, and a session control-approval consent gate.\n\nThis release also introduces the Standard (free) / Premium (licensed) split: Premium features unlock at runtime via SessionKitLicense.Activate(key) and degrade gracefully (or throw when explicitly constructed) without one. A Suite bundle key (SessionKit Premium + ServerKit) unlocks Premium too.\n\nPart of the RemoteViewer family — Connection = ConnectKit (free), Session = SessionKit, Server = ServerKit. Downloads, 5-minute quickstarts, and Premium/Suite keys: https://www.remote-viewer.com/downloads",
